# 📘 Topics Covered

## 1. Packages in Java

### Introduction
A package in Java is a collection of related classes and interfaces organized together.

### Advantages of Packages
- Avoids naming conflicts
- Provides access protection
- Makes code reusable and organized

---

# 📦 Defining a Package

## Syntax

```java
package package_name;
````

## Example

```java id="a1p2k3"
package mypackage;

class Demo {
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Package Example");
    }
}
```

---

# 📥 Importing Packages and Classes

Packages and classes can be imported using the `import` keyword.

## Syntax

```java
import package_name.class_name;
```

## Example

```java id="b4q5r6"
import java.util.Scanner;
```

---

# 🛤 Path and Class Path

## Path

* Specifies location of Java tools like `javac` and `java`

## Class Path

* Specifies location of compiled `.class` files and packages

### Example

```bash id="c7s8t9"
set classpath=.;
```

---

# 🔐 Access Control in Java

## Access Modifiers

| Modifier  | Access Level                             |
| --------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| public    | Accessible everywhere                    |
| private   | Accessible only within class             |
| protected | Accessible within package and subclasses |
| default   | Accessible within package                |

