# ⚠ Exception Handling in Java

## Introduction

Exception handling is used to handle runtime errors and maintain normal program execution.

---

# 🧱 Hierarchy of Standard Exception Classes

```text id="d1u2v3"
Throwable
 ├── Error
 └── Exception
      ├── IOException
      ├── ArithmeticException
      ├── NullPointerException
      └── ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
```

---

# 🔑 Keywords `throw` and `throws`

## throw

Used to explicitly throw an exception.

```java id="e4w5x6"
throw new ArithmeticException("Error");
```

## throws

Used to declare exceptions in method definition.

```java id="f7y8z9"
void display() throws IOException {
}
```

---

# 🧪 try, catch, and finally Blocks

## Example

```java id="g1h2i3"
class ExceptionDemo {

    public static void main(String args[]) {

        try {
            int a = 10 / 0;
        }

        catch(ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Exception Caught");
        }

        finally {
            System.out.println("Finally Block Executed");
        }
    }
}
```

---

# 🔄 Multiple Catch Clauses

## Example

```java id="j4k5l6"
try {
    int arr[] = new int[5];
    arr[10] = 50;
}

catch(ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
    System.out.println("Array Error");
}

catch(Exception e) {
    System.out.println("General Exception");
}
```

---

# 🧩 Class Throwable

* Root class for all exceptions and errors
* Provides methods like:

  * `getMessage()`
  * `printStackTrace()`

---

# ✅ Checked Exceptions

Checked exceptions are checked during compile time.

## Examples

* IOException
* SQLException

---

# ❌ Unchecked Exceptions

Unchecked exceptions occur during runtime.

## Examples

* ArithmeticException
* NullPointerException
* ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException

---

# 💻 Sample Program

```java id="m7n8o9"
import java.util.Scanner;

class Divide {

    public static void main(String args[]) {

        try {

            int a = 10;
            int b = 0;

            int c = a / b;

            System.out.println(c);
        }

        catch(ArithmeticException e) {

            System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero");
        }

        finally {

            System.out.println("Program Executed");
        }
    }
}
```

